Found in the k19 fidelity audit (pre-existing, outside the k19 diff).

Upstream environment.js:213 `throw new Error('template names must be a string: ' + name)` -- `+` runs JS ToString on name. Port lib/Text/Nunjucks/Environment.pm:318 concatenates with Perl `.`.

Oracle (renderString, any loader):
- `{% include u %}` (u missing) -> `template names must be a string: undefined`; port: `... string: ` (empty, plus a "Use of uninitialized value" warning)
- `{% include n %}` with n = null -> `... string: null`; port: `... string: Text::Nunjucks::Runtime::None=SCALAR(0x...)`
- `{% include true %}` -> `... string: true`; port: `... string: 1`
- `{% include [1,2] %}` -> `... string: 1,2`; port: `... string: ARRAY(0x...)`
- `{% include {} %}` -> `... string: [object Object]`; port: `... string: Hash::Ordered=ARRAY(0x...)`
- `{% include 5 %}` -> `... string: 5` in both.

Fix: build the message with Runtime's JS ToString (the seam copy_safeness / _js_to_string uses) instead of Perl concatenation. No corpus case pins it (grep "template names must be" t/corpus/ is empty): add the five cases above to t/corpus/ via maint/corpus-regen.

